WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.180
Before you use the dashboard, confirm that you opened the correct workspace and account.

2
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.700
The public demo uses sample data and shows features beyond some editions.

3
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.760
In your own workspace, check whether the environment is testnet or mainnet.

4
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.500
Never interpret the demo balances as your account balance.

5
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:31.220
Account value represents the trading account, while available balance shows what is available after margin and other constraints.

6
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.460
An agent allocation is a software budget, not another deposit.

7
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:42.960
Compare the dashboard with the same account and network on Hyperliquid before allocating funds.

8
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.260
Open Agents.

9
00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.040
Each card represents a configured strategy instance.

10
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.460
Read its strategy, market, state and latest decision before using any control.

11
00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:04.160
Active means the strategy can evaluate opportunities; it does not promise an immediate trade.

12
00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:08.880
A missing signal or risk restriction can correctly prevent an entry.

13
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.640
A position is actual exposure.

14
00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:21.100
An order is an instruction that may be open, partly filled, filled or canceled.

15
00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.680
One agent can be active with no position.

16
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.820
Review positions and open orders together.

17
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.060
When a status looks inconsistent, compare the venue before issuing another instruction.

18
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:43.700
Use System Status to check the services and the latest update times available in your edition.

19
00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:48.520
A page that loads is not proof that prices or orders are current.

20
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:57.340
If updates stop, avoid adding new exposure and contact support with the time, workspace and a redacted error.

21
00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:09.480
Your first checkpoint is simple: identify the account, network, agent status, positions and latest update.

22
00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:14.580
Practice navigating without starting an agent or signing a transaction.

23
00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:19.620
Continue to the next lesson when you can explain what each of those fields means.
